NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid Query can also be used with Solid's "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.solidjs.com/reference/components/suspense","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Suspense"}]},{"type":"text","value":" API's."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To do that you need to wrap your suspendable component with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Suspense"},{"type":"text","value":" component provided by Solid"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Suspense } from 'solid-js'\n;<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSpinner />}>\n  <SuspendableComponent />\n</Suspense>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can use async "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"suspense"},{"type":"text","value":" function that is provided by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"solid-query"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nconst todoFetcher = async () =>\n  await fetch('https://jsonplaceholder.cypress.io/todos').then((response) =>\n    response.json(),\n  )\n\nfunction SuspendableComponent() {\n  const todosQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: todoFetcher,\n  }))\n\n  // Accessing todosQuery.data directly inside a <Suspense> boundary\n  // automatically triggers suspension until data is ready\n  return <div>Data: {JSON.stringify(todosQuery.data)}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"fetch-on-render-vs-render-as-you-fetch","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fetch-on-render vs Render-as-you-fetch"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Out of the box, Solid Query in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"suspense"},{"type":"text","value":" mode works really well as a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fetch-on-render"}]},{"type":"text","value":" solution with no additional configuration. This means that when your components attempt to mount, they will trigger query fetching and suspend, but only once you have imported them and mounted them. If you want to take it to the next level and implement a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render-as-you-fetch"}]},{"type":"text","value":" model, we recommend implementing "},{"type":"link","href":"./prefetching","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefetching"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on routing callbacks and/or user interactions events to start loading queries before they are mounted and hopefully even before you start importing or mounting their parent components."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"fetch-on-render-vs-render-as-you-fetch","text":"Fetch-on-render vs Render-as-you-fetch","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nSolid Query can also be used with Solid's [Suspense](https://docs.solidjs.com/reference/components/suspense) API's.\n\nTo do that you need to wrap your suspendable component with `Suspense` component provided by Solid\n\n```tsx\nimport { Suspense } from 'solid-js'\n;<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSpinner />}>\n  <SuspendableComponent />\n</Suspense>\n```\n\nYou can use async `suspense` function that is provided by `solid-query`.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nconst todoFetcher = async () =>\n  await fetch('https://jsonplaceholder.cypress.io/todos').then((response) =>\n    response.json(),\n  )\n\nfunction SuspendableComponent() {\n  const todosQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: todoFetcher,\n  }))\n\n  // Accessing todosQuery.data directly inside a <Suspense> boundary\n  // automatically triggers suspension until data is ready\n  return <div>Data: {JSON.stringify(todosQuery.data)}</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Fetch-on-render vs Render-as-you-fetch\n\nOut of the box, Solid Query in `suspense` mode works really well as a **Fetch-on-render** solution with no additional configuration. This means that when your components attempt to mount, they will trigger query fetching and suspend, but only once you have imported them and mounted them. If you want to take it to the next level and implement a **Render-as-you-fetch** model, we recommend implementing [Prefetching](./prefetching) on routing callbacks and/or user interactions events to start loading queries before they are mounted and hopefully even before you start importing or mounting their parent components.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: suspense\ntitle: Suspense\n---\n\nSolid Query can also be used with Solid's [Suspense](https://docs.solidjs.com/reference/components/suspense) API's.\n\nTo do that you need to wrap your suspendable component with `Suspense` component provided by Solid\n\n```tsx\nimport { Suspense } from 'solid-js'\n;<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSpinner />}>\n  <SuspendableComponent />\n</Suspense>\n```\n\nYou can use async `suspense` function that is provided by `solid-query`.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nconst todoFetcher = async () =>\n  await fetch('https://jsonplaceholder.cypress.io/todos').then((response) =>\n    response.json(),\n  )\n\nfunction SuspendableComponent() {\n  const todosQuery = useQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: todoFetcher,\n  }))\n\n  // Accessing todosQuery.data directly inside a <Suspense> boundary\n  // automatically triggers suspension until data is ready\n  return <div>Data: {JSON.stringify(todosQuery.data)}</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Fetch-on-render vs Render-as-you-fetch\n\nOut of the box, Solid Query in `suspense` mode works really well as a **Fetch-on-render** solution with no additional configuration. This means that when your components attempt to mount, they will trigger query fetching and suspend, but only once you have imported them and mounted them. If you want to take it to the next level and implement a **Render-as-you-fetch** model, we recommend implementing [Prefetching](./prefetching) on routing callbacks and/or user interactions events to start loading queries before they are mounted and hopefully even before you start importing or mounting their parent components.\n"}
